; specs/course_recipe/vibecoding-plan.t27 -- the plan of the course "Vibecoding from zero with t27"
; Read with the recipe (course-27.t27, skill course-27): this file is steps "pick", "shape" and
; the lesson half of "specs" for the new course. It is a plan, not the course: the course spec
; (specs/course/vibecoding.t27), its Russian contract and the 27 widgets are built from it, one
; lane per module (BEFORE_SHIP below). Compile and test with the site's own compiler:
;   cd apps/website && node ~/.claude/skills/course-27/scripts/t27check.mjs specs/course_recipe/vibecoding-plan.t27
; ASCII only, English only.

; WHERE THE WORDS COME FROM: the book "The Vibecoder's Bible" (Russian: Biblia vaibkodera) by the
; owner, kept as an Obsidian vault ("Agentic Vibecoding", iCloud) and mirrored in the repository
; gHashTag/999-multibots-telegraf under vaults/vibecoding. The plan keeps the book's order for a
; reader who starts from zero: why, the desk, git, prompting, the working loop, checking, an agent's
; parts, a first bot, an own project. The book's chapter names are kept in LESSON_BOOK in English.

; WHAT THE COURSE TAKES FROM THE BOOK AND WHAT IT LEAVES: it takes the method (describe, run,
; read, fix), the terms, the git and prompting chapters and the project roadmaps. It leaves every
; market figure, income range, success story and "percent of graduates" line: a number on a course
; page comes from a spec constant, a test the player ran or a recording (recipe rule
; numbers-from-runs), and none of those lines has one. The book's TypeScript and Python snippets
; are not carried over either: every lesson spec is t27 (owner's rule: only t27), and the lesson
; about a bot shows the spec a bot is generated from, not a hand-written bot.

; WHAT IS DIFFERENT FROM A BOOK CHAPTER: every lesson opens ONE widget (a tool driven by a
; compiled t27 spec, id vc-*, unique across all courses) and ONE t27 spec the reader runs in the
; player. The widget is where a beginner does the thing the lesson names (plants a bug, reads a
; diff, splits a prompt); the spec is the same idea as code that has a test.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module vibecoding_plan;

pub const KIND : str = "course-plan";
pub const SCHEMA_VERSION : u8 = 1;
pub const ID : str = "vibecoding";
; Course 11 of specs/course/courses.t27 is the last live one (queen-and-hive); the new course is
